<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles II of Spain</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1661">1661</a>–<a href="/years/1700">1700</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> was the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> king of Spain, reigning from 1665 to 1700. Sickly and childless, he presided over a period of economic weakness and military losses to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. His will left the throne to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-v-of-spain">Philip of Anjou</a>, grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a>, which brought the Bourbon dynasty to Spain and led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-ii-of-spain.jpg" alt="Charles II of Spain" width="320" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Juan Carreño de Miranda · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Juan_de_Miranda_Carreno_002.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>When the childless <b>Charles II</b> died in 1700, the War of the Spanish Succession brought the Bourbon Philip V to the throne.</blockquote><a href="/empire/crown-of-castile">Crown of Castile · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Under the sickly <b>Charles II</b> (r. 1665–1700) France took Franche-Comté in 1678 and further towns in the Netherlands, though historians such as Henry Kamen have argued that parts of Spain’s economy began to recover in the later seventeenth century.</blockquote><a href="/empire/habsburg-spain">Habsburg Spain · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>The war had begun over the throne of <b>Charles II of Spain</b>, who died in 1700 without children.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/july-24">24 July in history</a></li><li><blockquote>A papal conclave elected Cardinal Giovanni Albani as Clement XI after a month's deadlock that ended with the death of the childless <b>Charles II of Spain</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/november-23">23 November in history</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Charles II</b>, last of Habsburg Spain, left the throne to Philip of Anjou, grandson of Louis XIV, who became Philip V in 1700.</blockquote><a href="/state/bourbon-spain">Bourbon Spain</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrid">Madrid</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrid">Madrid</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=40.42,-3.7&amp;year=1686" aria-label="Madrid on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4459 719 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Charles II of Spain"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4909 989h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4909 989h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=40.42,-3.7&amp;year=1686">What was here in 1686? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
